-# Code Action Provider Sample
+# Release Checklist
 
-This sample shows how to provide code actions in the editor. Code actions are used to implement quick fixes and [refactoring](https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/editor/refactoring) in VS Code.
+Group Markdown changelog issues by file in the **Release Checklist** view in
+Explorer. Open an issue to jump to its line and use **Add Unreleased section**
+when the heading is missing.
 
-The sample uses the [`CodeActionProvider`](https://code.visualstudio.com/api/references/vscode-api#CodeActionProvider) api to implement a simple set of code actions that convert `:)` to a smiley emoji in markdown files:
+Use **Release Checklist: Scan Workspace Changelogs** to audit closed files.
+The command scans up to 200 matching files outside dependency folders, using
+UTF-8 and a 1 MiB limit per file. Rescan after changing a closed file on disk.
+Open editors show their current contents, including unsaved changes.
 
-![Emoji code actions](example.gif)
+## Development
 
-Second example of code action provider shows how to associate code actions with diagnostic (e.g. compilation) problems.
+Run `npm ci`, `npm run compile`, `npm run lint`, and
+`node --test tests/*.test.mjs`. Use **Run Release Checklist Tests** in VS Code
+to run the extension-host integration checks.
 
